  "spec": "DESIGN.md — installations, the machine seam, standalone save cards (issue #181)",
  "description": "Whole fixture machines in; the canonical SavefilePlacement serialization (atlas/contract.py) out, asserted with exact equality — for catalogue entries whose launch command names a standalone emulator a packaged save card covers. The card is the thin cited half (atlas/data/standalone_saves.json); the resolver reads the emulator's own configuration the way the emulator does, at the revision the arrangement ships (Dolphin 2603a). Root kind is emulator_directory: no frontend hands these emulators a save root.",
  "vectors": [
    {
      "name": "dolphin-keeps-one-gci-folder-per-region-and-the-region-is-a-hole",
      "rationale": "The GCI-folder device sits in slot A (Dolphin.ini [Core] SlotA = 8, the registered default), so a GameCube save is one .gci file in <GC user>/<region>/Card A — named from the save's own directory entry, which no read of the content path recovers. The answer's dir keeps the <region> segment as a hole a caller with metadata fills, while the groups list all three region trees so a caller without it still sees the whole candidate set. RetroDECK reroutes the region trees with symlinks; the emulator-view dirs are the answer's.",
